### Git Projects

Milestone vs label. 
A label is a tag for categorising by kind (bug, documentation). 
A milestone is for grouping by goal, and it tracks completion. Labels don't have dates or progress.

Milestone vs iteration. 
A milestone lives on the repository, is one-off, and has a single due date. 
An iteration lives in a project as a custom field and repeats on a cadence. 
Sprints → iteration. 
A release with a deadline → milestone.
